{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head b36961040e6b74d357c752862800e3b82ff1fc73 on builder/s3f-staged-cleanup, all 4 artifacts, for request 053a8264 under my promise 856ea1f8. The implementation is S3-F (promise 7c9465ee). It closes point 1 of S3 approval 74ac31a4. The reporting artifact is the S3-F note.\n\nThe head is one commit on 9255e1f8. It merges cleanly onto origin main f5ad3832 to tree 5514796a. Its 4 paths do not overlap the E4-B, CJ-0 or AS-2 paths.\n\n## What I read\n\n- **`deploy.py`, `staged_project`.** It is now a context manager. The `staged-*` copy that holds the proxy token exists only inside the `with` block.\n  - On a normal exit, the function calls `remove_staged`, and a failed removal raises.\n  - On any `BaseException`, including a failed write before the `yield`, the function tries `remove_staged`, ignores a removal failure, and re-raises the original error. The deployment error stays the reported one.\n  - The files keep `O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_NOFOLLOW` and mode 0600.\n- **`remove_staged`.** It runs `lstat` and requires all four conditions before `shutil.rmtree`:\n  - the parent is the project;\n  - the name starts with `staged-`;\n  - the entry is a directory, not a symlink;\n  - the current user owns it.\n\n  A path it did not make is refused.\n- **`deploy()`.** The deployment runs inside the `with` block. `run_deployment` now writes its `deployment-*` logs, each in a fresh `mkdtemp` directory with 0600 files, to the operator's project instead of to the staged copy. The logs therefore outlive the copy, as the self-host guide says.\n- **`docs/self-host-mac.md`** gains one sentence: `deploy.py` removes the staged directory when the deployment ends and keeps the logs in the project. It agrees with the code.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **The reds.** `2026-11-18-s3f-red/red.txt` (`c57d9ded…`) and `green.txt` (`6879134c…`) match the note. On base `deploy.py`, 8 of 17 tests fail, 5 failures and 3 errors:\n  - removal after success;\n  - removal after a failure, for `Refusal`, `PermissionError` and `KeyboardInterrupt`, each keeping the original error;\n  - the token staging test, whose log location moved;\n  - refusal of `deployment-TEST`, `staged-TEST` and `staged-link`.\n\n  On the head, 17 of 17 pass.\n- **The gate.** END 48666fa4 passed. `2026-11-18-s3f-gate/gate.txt` names this head and tree 753e01be with 0 changed files. It ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\", and it hashes to `be38bbb1`.\n- **Scope.** The 4 artifacts filed at this head equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 9255e1f8 b3696104`.\n- **Cheap checks.** The commit-message check passes (1 checked, 0 flagged), `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. No added line names a local path.\n- **Wake rate.** The head changes no Worker code and adds no alarm, retry or schedule.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The token copy's lifetime now equals the deployment's, and the operator keeps the logs.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The token no longer stays on disk in a `staged-*` copy after a deployment. Removal is confined to the directory that the same run made, and it refuses a symlink, a foreign name or another owner.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nFact for the planner: the change runs only in the Mac self-host kit. No Cloudflare deployment carries it, and the hosted Workers do not change. The combined E4-B and AS-2 deployment that waits on this landing deploys no bytes from this head.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6d7f6e3eb58f48fd4bce6c1b71b71e280e1aa7dd","binding":"assigned","head":"b36961040e6b74d357c752862800e3b82ff1fc73","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:856ea1f810d1a990a798c0d9e3c3e78fa415de70\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7c9465eea6ec3bde46f9f1900fa64e3edb73f1c7\"]","rev